# DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Babylonian Square Root of 2 (YBC 7289)
# Difficulty: Exemplar
# Concept: Historical Archaeology & YBC 7289
# Mode: Scholar (Latin transliteration)
#
# Purpose:
#   Computes the Babylonian approximation of sqrt(2) (1;24,51,10) using iterative
#   Heron-Babylonian reciprocal calculations from tablet YBC 7289.
#
# Expected Output:
#   Babylonian sqrt(2) approximation:
#   1 + 195025/470832
#   Square with side 30 has diagonal:
#   42 + 33461/78472

problem

    initial-estimate : 1;30
    steps : 3
    target-diagonal : 30

    approx :
        initial-estimate
        steps
        apply babylonian-sqrt

    diagonal :
        target-diagonal
        approx
        multiply

recipe babylonian-sqrt start iterations:

    x : start
    two : 2
    half : 0;30

    consider step from 1 through iterations:
        next-x :
            x
            two
            x
            divide
            add
            half
            multiply
        x : next-x

    determine x

result

    output "Babylonian sqrt(2) approximation:"
    output approx

    output "Square with side 30 has diagonal:"
    output diagonal
